# Contributing to Simple Interest Calculator

## Welcome!

All contributions, bug reports, bug fixes, documentation improvements, enhancements, and ideas are welcome.

We appreciate your interest in contributing to this project. This document provides guidelines and instructions for contributing.

## How to Contribute

### Reporting Bugs

When reporting bugs, please include:
* A clear, descriptive title
* A detailed description of the bug
* Steps to reproduce the issue
* Expected behavior
* Actual behavior
* Your environment (OS, shell, etc.)

### Suggesting Enhancements

Enhancement suggestions are always welcome! Please include:
* A clear, descriptive title
* A detailed description of the enhancement
* Why this enhancement would be useful
* Possible implementation details (if you have ideas)

### Documentation Improvements

Documentation improvements help everyone understand and use the project better. You can:
* Fix typos and grammatical errors
* Clarify existing documentation
* Add missing documentation
* Improve code comments

### Bug Fixes

If you'd like to fix a bug:
1. Fork the repository
2. Create a new branch for your fix
3. Make your changes
4. Test your changes thoroughly
5. Submit a pull request with a clear description

### Feature Implementation

To implement a new feature:
1. Discuss your idea by opening an issue first
2. Wait for feedback from maintainers
3. Fork the repository
4. Create a new branch for your feature
5. Implement the feature with clear commits
6. Add or update tests and documentation
7. Submit a pull request

## Development Setup

1. Fork the repository
2. Clone your fork locally:
```bash
   git clone https://github.com/AbdulSamad99661/simple-interest-calculator111111.git
```
3. Create a branch for your changes:
```bash
   git checkout -b main
```
4. Make your changes
5. Test your changes
6. Commit with clear, descriptive messages
7. Push to your fork
8. Submit a pull request

## Commit Messages

Please use clear and descriptive commit messages:
* Use the present tense ("Add feature" not "Added feature")
* Use the imperative mood ("Move cursor to..." not "Moves cursor to...")
* Limit the first line to 72 characters or less
* Reference issues and pull requests liberally after the first line

## Pull Request Process

1. Update documentation and tests with your changes
2. Ensure all tests pass
3. Provide a clear description of your changes
4. Reference any related issues
5. Be patient and open to feedback from reviewers

## Code of Conduct

This project and everyone participating in it is governed by our Code of Conduct. By participating, you are expected to uphold this code.

## Questions?

If you have any questions, feel free to open an issue or reach out to the maintainers.

Thank you for contributing!
